+# Review Request — M026 Geometry Diagnostics and Autonomous Tic-Tac-Toe
+
+## Review ID
+
+```text
+review.m026.geometry-diagnostics-and-autonomous-tic-tac-toe
+```
+
+## Applicability
+
+```text
+level: required
+blocking: true
+classes: visual, UX, artifact-quality
+```
+
+## Subject
+
+Review geometry authoring diagnostics and the Autonomous Tic-Tac-Toe consumer after automated semantic validation.
+
+## Required evidence
+
+- geometry inspection, preview, diagnostics, comparison, and all-shape capture;
+- Signal Passage geometry diagnostic run;
+- tic-tac-toe board, thinking, mark, takeover, invalid selection, win/draw, and reset captures;
+- generated-sound linkage report and cue inventory;
+- deterministic AI, human takeover, and save-during-thinking results;
+- Linux export launch;
+- M026 performance report;
+- consumer-boundary decision report;
+- current non-review receipts.
+
+## Approval criteria
+
+Diagnostics are understandable/actionable; board cells, marks, current participant, and ownership are readable; takeover and selection are comprehensible; thinking/placing/result/reset states are distinguishable; sounds/animation/particles support state; boundary decisions match evidence; no severe visual/UX defect blocks consumer-validation use.
+
+## Record and re-review
+
+Store under `.review/records/` with revision and evidence fingerprints. Re-review on diagnostic format/severity, contrast policy, board mapping, takeover interaction, thinking/mark/particle presentation, linkage semantics, boundary classifications, or evidence changes.
